{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The sense: I will be still concerning the Shekhinah that stood." "<b>And I will look.</b> And I will see." "<b>My dwelling-place.</b> It is Jerusalem." "<b>Like heat.</b> Air." "<b>A clear light upon me.</b> After rain, as in \"He scatters His light\" (Job 37:11), for the sun is called light, and likewise the moon, for so it is written: \"to Him who made great lights\" (Psalms 136:7); they are the cause of rain by the decree of HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:11.509741876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}